From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: explorer reads the graphics driver from HKLM

Multi-user debt D4. Which Wine graphics driver to load is a fact about the
machine, but explorer read it only from HKCU\Software\Wine\Drivers, so every
user's session wrote its own copy of a machine-level setting -- and a second
user inherited nothing until their own session wrote it.

explorer now reads HKLM\Software\Wine\Drivers\Graphics first -- set once by the
administrator (sg-session's sg-prefix-init writes it as SYSTEM) -- and a user's
HKCU may still override it, the same layering DllOverrides uses (patch 0009).
Upstream's HKCU-only behaviour is otherwise unchanged; with neither key set the
built-in default list is used as before.
--- a/programs/explorer/desktop.c
+++ b/programs/explorer/desktop.c
@@ -1008,11 +1008,26 @@
     {
         lstrcpyW( buffer, default_driver );
 
+        /* Stained Glass OS (multi-user debt D4): which graphics driver to load
+         * is a fact about the machine, so it is read from HKLM first -- set once
+         * by the administrator -- and a user's HKCU may still override it, as
+         * with DllOverrides (patch 0009). Upstream reads HKCU only, which made
+         * every user's session write its own copy. */
+        /* @@ Wine registry key: HKLM\Software\Wine\Drivers */
+        if (!RegOpenKeyW( HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE, L"Software\\Wine\\Drivers", &hkey ))
+        {
+            DWORD count = sizeof(buffer);
+            if (RegQueryValueExW( hkey, L"Graphics", 0, NULL, (LPBYTE)buffer, &count ))
+                lstrcpyW( buffer, default_driver );
+            RegCloseKey( hkey );
+        }
         /* @@ Wine registry key: HKCU\Software\Wine\Drivers */
         if (!RegOpenKeyW( HKEY_CURRENT_USER, L"Software\\Wine\\Drivers", &hkey ))
         {
-            DWORD count = sizeof(buffer);
-            RegQueryValueExW( hkey, L"Graphics", 0, NULL, (LPBYTE)buffer, &count );
+            WCHAR user[MAX_PATH];
+            DWORD count = sizeof(user);
+            if (!RegQueryValueExW( hkey, L"Graphics", 0, NULL, (LPBYTE)user, &count ))
+                lstrcpyW( buffer, user );
             RegCloseKey( hkey );
         }
     }
